      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T18:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"ap_pwr_data_##n\" struct couldn\u0027t be \"const\" because it\ncontains \"struct ap_power_ev_callback cb\", which is mutated by\n\"ap_power_ev_init_callback\" and \"ap_power_ev_add_callback\". To address this,\nI split the struct into an immutable \"ap_power_events_config\" (holding `gpios`\nand \u0027num_gpios\u0027, declared \u0027const\u0027) and a mutable \"ap_power_events_data\"\n(holding only \u0027cb\u0027 and a \u0027const\u0027 pointer back to the config). The handler and\ninit function are updated accordingly.",
