        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T17:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you add a setup function that checks that all the GPIOs initialize as de-asserted? This will run once before any of these test cases. This might be unreliable if power sequencing code immediately starts up, though.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "9db16a0307a0eab000b166b65b49e08d8cc78a29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cfccd10_10871a09",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/drivers/ap_power_events/src/ap_power_events.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1537933
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-03T18:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added the setup function initially, but found some reliability concerns which proved correct while testing. The test suite runs twice — once on the initial boot (where it passed) and again after the EC firmware triggers a reboot via\n\"auto_power_on set due to reset flags\". On the second boot, the EC power state\nmachine fires AP_POWER_STARTUP before the suite setup function runs, asserting\nboth GPIOs. This caused the setup\u0027s zassert_false to fail, putting the suite\ninto ZTEST_RESULT_SUITE_FAIL and failing all 5 tests.\n\nSo I removed the setup function and kept NULL instead. Added before function which handles resetting GPIO state before every test, so tests remain correct across both boots.",
      "parentUuid": "831adb22_3cae6988",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 39
      },
